condition_name: Nephrotic Syndrome
condition_slug: nephrotic-syndrome
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "A clinical complex characterized by the following: Proteinuria of 3.5 g per 24 hours, Hypoalbuminaemia, Generalized oedema, Hyperlipidaemia, Lipiduria, Hypercoagulability."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[2]: Generalized body swelling,Passage of frothy urine
investigations[4]: "Blood: Serum proteins, Serum lipids","Urine: Urinalysis, 24-hour urine collection for protein estimation",Abdominal ultrasound scan,Renal biopsy
treatment:
  goals[2]: Reduce proteinuria,Eradicate peripheral oedema
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[3]: Diuretics e.g. loop diuretics like furosemide,Glucocorticoids (e.g. prednisolone),Cytotoxic drugs (e.g. cyclophosphamide) in some steroid-resistant cases
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[3]: Congestive heart failure,Decompensated chronic liver disease,Protein losing enteropathy
complications[6]: Peripheral arterial or venous thrombosis,Acceleration of atherosclerosis,Protein malnutrition,Vitamin D deficiency,Increased susceptibility to infections,Iron-resistant microcytic hypochromic anaemia
prevention[2]: Avoid nephrotoxins,Treat bites and stings to prevent p haemolytic streptococcal infection
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null